PPT Master skill

Install:
  Prepare Node/pnpm and Git when missing; copy the named skill using skills CLI. Install system tools and an isolated Python environment from the installed skill requirements; configure its Python entry point.

Upgrade:
  Refresh only this skill and run the same runtime preparation steps.

Status:
  Report local skill files, document/media/font package versions, core Python imports and entry-point presence.

Requirements:
  Ubuntu, APT and a regular user with sudo access.

Configuration:
  Source: https://github.com/hugohe3/ppt-master
  Destination: ~/.agents/skills/ppt-master
  An existing Codex copy at $CODEX_HOME/skills/ppt-master becomes a link to this directory.
  CODEX_HOME defaults to ~/.codex.
  Python 3.12 environment: ~/.local/share/wsley/ppt-master/.venv
  An existing environment must use Python 3.12; incompatible or incomplete environments are preserved and reported.
  Python entry point: ~/.local/bin/ppt-master-python (specified in the installed SKILL.md).
  LibreOffice uses the same APT package as the libreoffice application module.
  External image-generation services require user-provided credentials.
  First skill backup: ${XDG_STATE_HOME:-$HOME/.local/state}/wsley/backups/.
  Codex authentication is configured separately.
